2026-01-02 19:17:56,614 - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/openai/v1/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-01eded39-192a-45a6-a73b-7ca30f94c69e', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': '\n        You are an expert Resume ATS Scanner and Career Coach.\n        \n        Job Description:\n        About the job\nUniphore is one of the largest B2B AI-native companies—decades-proven, built-for-scale and designed for the enterprise. The company drives business outcomes, across multiple industry verticals, and enables the largest global deployments.\n\nUniphore infuses AI into every part of the enterprise that impacts the customer. We deliver the only multimodal architecture centered on customers that combines Generative AI, Knowledge AI, Emotion AI, workflow automation and a co-pilot to guide you. We understand better than anyone how to capture voice, video and text and how to analyze all types of data.\n\nAs AI becomes more powerful, every part of the enterprise that impacts the customer will be disrupted. We believe the future will run on the connective tissue between people, machines and data: all in the service of creating the most human processes and experiences for customers and employees.\n\nJob Description\n\nAs a member of Uniphore’s Customer Success team, the Director of AI Customer Success will serve as strategic advisor to enterprise clients. This role blends executive-level client engagement, AI expertise, and a deep consulting background to ensure successful delivery, adoption, and long-term value realization of AI solutions. success capabilities. This role bridges the gap between technical capabilities and business needs, ensuring customers achieve their goals and maximize their return on investment. This role will focus primarily on our Customer Data Platforms (CDP) verticals of Martech and Adtech solutions.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\nThe Director of AI Customer Success will be the primary point of contact for Uniphore’s Enterprise Customers. In this role you will lead customer strategy by focusing on and following key facets of Customer Success Journey:\n\nDrive customer success outcomes by developing key Customer Success metrics such as Value Realization, key performance metrics, gross renewals rate, net retention, adoption, customer health, churn rate and customer health score. Work with Product and platform teams to improve SaaS telemetry and gain real time understanding of the pulse of the customer. \nDrive adoption, satisfaction, and long-term value through combining technical expertise and customer-facing skills.\nOwn executive-level relationships with key enterprise clients, serving as a trusted advisor for AI strategy, implementation, and value realization.\nLead complex customer engagements focused on deploying AI and data-driven solutions across business functions.\nDevelop tailored success plans and roadmaps that align AI capabilities with customer business objectives.\nPartner with Sales, Product, Engineering, and Delivery teams to ensure seamless implementation and continuous improvement.\nDrive customer adoption, expansion, and retention through strategic planning, outcomes tracking, and executive business reviews.\nEstablish best practices for enterprise customer success, from onboarding to renewal, with a focus on scalable AI impact.\nServe as a thought leader internally and externally on AI use cases, responsible AI practices, and digital transformation strategies.\nProvide feedback to product teams to influence the roadmap based on client needs and industry trends.\nChampioning the broader Uniphore Business AI Cloud Platform within your portfolio, driving adoption of the deep data and AI capabilities that enable business transformation.\nThis role will report to U.S. VP of Customer Success.\n\nRequired Qualifications\n\n8-10+ years of experience in consulting, customer success, or professional services, with a focus on enterprise technology solutions in the Customer Data Platforms (CDP) industry specifically focused on Martech and Adtech solutions.\n3-5+ years of experience working directly with AI products, platforms, or services in an advisory or delivery capacity.\n 5+ years’ experience engaging end users through C-Suite Executives, in both casual and formal professional settings.\nConsistent record of accomplishment in delivering ROI, exceeding retention, customer satisfaction, and advocacy targets.\nProven record of accomplishment of managing complex client relationships, leading multi-stakeholder engagements, and delivering measurable outcomes.\nExperience in enterprise verticals such as healthcare, financial services, manufacturing, or retail where AI has significant business impact.\nProven Track record of CDP AI Consultancy and driving growth and adoption of SAAS solutions.\nDeep understanding of CDP AI solution architectures, business applications of AI, and change management related to customer adoption.\nStrong strategic thinking, executive communication, and client-facing presence.\nExperience working with cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, GCP) and AI services (e.g., OpenAI, TensorFlow, Hugging Face, etc.).\nFamiliarity with enterprise software delivery lifecycles, success metrics, and ROI frameworks.\nExceptional organizational, presentation, and communication skills, both verbal and written \nClient-Centric & Empathetic: You genuinely care about your clients. You listen actively to their needs and put yourself in their shoes to anticipate issues and opportunities\nBachelor\'s or master\'s degree in business, Computer Science, Engineering, Data Science, or related field; MBA or advanced degree preferred.\nAbility to travel at least 25% of the time. \nThis role will report to the U. S. Vice President of Customer Success.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\nYou are fluent in the Martech and AdTech ecosystems. You have spent years navigating the complexity of marketing stacks and advertising tech—connecting systems, streamlining data flows, and unlocking real customer insights. Whether it is DMPs, CDPs, DSPs, or automation platforms, you know how it all fits together to drive performance.\nYou have led from the front with CDPs. With 6–10 years of hands-on experience in Customer Data Platforms for both B2B and B2C brands, you understand the strategic role they play in activating unified customer journeys across channels. You do not just support CDP adoption; you drive it, scale it, and optimize it.\nYou turn technology into outcomes. Your value lies in translating complex tools into clear, actionable strategies. You have advised enterprise clients on how to use data-driven marketing to directly impact KPIs like acquisition cost, engagement, retention, and revenue lift.\nYou have been the go-to for growth. You have partnered with marketers, media teams, and product leaders to implement scalable SaaS solutions that generate results. Your expertise ensures technology does not sit idle—it powers campaigns, unlocks insights, and fuels the business.\n\nHiring Range\n\n$186,900 - $257,000 - for Primary Location of USA - NY - New York\n\nThe specific rate will depend on the successful candidate\'s qualifications and prior experience.\n\nIn addition to competitive base pay, this position also includes an annual incentive opportunity based on target achievement, pre-IPO stock options, benefits including medical, dental, vision, 401(k) with a match, and more, plus generous paid time off, paid holidays, paid day off for your birthday and other paid leave policies to support employees through all phases of life.\n\nLocation preference:\n\nUSA - CA - Palo Alto, USA - NY - New York\n\nUniphore is an equal opportunity employer committed to diversity in the workplace. We evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, disability, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.\n\nFor more information on how Uniphore uses AI to unify—and humanize—every enterprise experience, please visit\u202fwww.uniphore.com.\n        \n        Resume Content:\n        PAVAN HARESH \n+1 214-430-6317| paven026@gmail.com| linkedin.com/in/impavan/| Texas| USA(Open to Relocate) \n \nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY \nAI Strategy and Enterprise Transformation Leader with 12+ years of experience driving large-scale AI adoption, product innovation, and \nmeasurable enterprise value across Healthcare, Retail, BFSI, and Energy verticals and cross industry functions such as F&A, HR, Procurement, \nlegal, marketing, Supply Chain. Proven commercial and delivery track record generating $250M+ pipeline, closing $50M+ revenue, and enabling \n$1B+ in business impact through AI modernization, platform development, and GTM execution. Deep expertise in Generative AI, Agentic AI, RAG \necosystems, Conversational AI, Knowledge Intelligence, and enterprise AI platforms across Azure, AWS, and Google Cloud combining hands-on \ntechnical credibility with strong product leadership and C-Suite partnership. Recognized for building scalable AI platforms, establishing \nresponsible AI governance in regulated environments, and leading cross-functional engineering, data, and product teams to deliver secure, \ncompliant, and high-impact AI solutions at enterprise scale. \n \nEDUCATION \nVisvesvaraya Technological University (VTU) \nBachelor of Engineering, Computer Science   \n \n \n \n \n                                      August 2009 - July 2013 \n \nEXPERIENCE \nWipro \nSenior Product Manager & Practice Partner  \n \n \n \n \n                                  November 2023 - Present \nPlano, TX, USA \n• \nDirected AI strategy and GTM execution across Healthcare, Retail, Life Sciences, Telecom verticals using ML/DL, GenAI, Agentic AI, and \nknowledge intelligence platforms, driving ~$250M opportunity pipeline and ~$50M+ in closed revenue. \n• \nPartnered with C-Suite leadership to build enterprise AI modernization roadmaps spanning clinical operations, regulatory workflows, \nand automation programs, aligning technology investments to measurable business outcomes and scalable value realization. \n• \nEstablished a large-scale AI Center of Excellence for a major U.S. healthcare payer leveraging GenAI, decision intelligence, and \nautomated workflows, reducing manual reviews by ~40%, improving claim turnaround by 25–30%, and delivering $50M+ annual cost \nefficiencies. \n• \nArchitected behavioral claims audit automation with Multi Agent System using Azure, Langchain stack across 5M+ annual claims, \nenabling real-time fraud and compliance anomaly detection and reducing manual intervention while increasing audit accuracy and \noperational assurance. \n• \nBuilt an enterprise Agentic AI system and workflow orchestration POC on Azure/Autogen stack to automate plan build and onboarding \nprocesses, cutting configuration cycles by 60%. \n• \nDesigned GenAI SOP conversational agent on Azure to find accurate answers from relevant SOP clauses, enhancing Dental First pass \nand adjustments claims processor\'s efficiency by 30%. \nProduct Manager \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n                      February 2022 - November 2023 \nLondon, UK \n• \nOwned global product roadmap and delivery for AI-powered Knowledge Platforms built using Azure Cognitive Search (BM25 + \nSemantic + Hybrid Search), indexing 80M+ documents across 12TB of enterprise content and improving knowledge access and \ndecisioning for ENU client. \n• \nLed agile delivery as Product Manager and Scrum Master, managing sprints, stakeholder priorities, and platform enhancements to \nensure predictable delivery, product adoption, and measurable business outcomes. \n• \nOversaw enterprise migration from Apache Solr to Azure Cognitive Search, enhancing scalability, search results relevancy and \naccuracy, improving search efficiency and operational resilience. \n• \nDefined and executed responsible AI governance practices aligned to regulatory frameworks, ensuring secure, compliant, and risk-\naware AI adoption. \n• \nAdvanced GTM execution for AI offerings in regulated industries, guiding customers from PoC to full enterprise rollout, driving tangible \nROI and operational modernization. \n \nSolution Architect \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n        August 2019 - February 2022 \nBengaluru, India \n• \nDesigned and implemented end-to-end architecture and delivery of Contact Center Transformation and Knowledge Intelligence \nplatforms on Azure, aligning technical solutions to business goals, scalability requirements, and security standards for Manufacturing \nand Telecom clients in UK geo. \n• \nArchitected migration of Conversational AI platforms from IBM Cloud to Azure using NLP frameworks and cloud re-engineering, \nimproving reliability, performance, and cost efficiency with minimal downtime. \n• \nCollaborated with business, vendor, and technical stakeholders to define architecture blueprints, delivery plans, and execution \ngovernance, ensuring program stability, stakeholder alignment, and successful deployment. \n \n \n \nUniphore \nSenior Software Engineer  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n                         November 2018 - August 2019 \nBengaluru, India \n• \nBuilt advanced NLP and conversational AI solutions for healthcare client using deep learning (Bi-LSTM, entity extraction) deployed in \nsecure cloud environments, enabling automation, improved service quality, and operational efficiency. \n• \nLed secure deployment and lifecycle management of ML/DL models, ensuring reliability, compliance, and sustained performance. \nPlankton Solutions \nSenior Software Engineer \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n          June 2016 - November 2018 \nBengaluru, India \n• \nDesigned and deployed enterprise chatbot and analytics platforms using AI/ML and AWS cloud infrastructure, enhancing customer \nexperience and operational intelligence. \n• \nLed presales engineering, client solution design, and analytics delivery, supporting successful client adoption and market-\naligned AI deployment. \nTech Mahindra \nSenior Project Engineer \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n               January 2014 - June 2016 \nBengaluru, India \n• \nDelivered enterprise automation solutions across QA, UI, and reporting for Fortune 500 clients using Python, Selenium, Appium tools, \nimproving operational efficiency, stability, and risk governance. \n \nCERTIFICATION \n• \nAgentic AI - DeepLearning.AI \n• \nGenerative AI Engineer Associate - Databricks \n• \nGoogle Cloud GenAI Level 3 - Wipro AI Academy \n• \nAI Product Management - Duke University \n• \nProject Management - Google \n• \nAzure AI Developer Associate - Microsoft \n• \nAzure AI Fundamentals - Microsoft \n \nSKILLS \n• \nAI/ML: Azure OpenAI, AWS Bedrock, Google Vertex AI, Databricks, Agentspace, LangChain, AutoGen, RAG architectures, Multi-agent \nsystems, MLOps (Azure ML, MLflow) \n• \nCloud & Data: Azure, AWS, Google Cloud, Snowflake, Vector DBs (Pinecone, Milvus. ChromaDB) \n• \nSoftware Development: Python, Langchain, REST APIs (Flask/FastAPI), JavaScript, Docker, CI/CD, Git \n• \nEnterprise Platforms: Salesforce, MS Dynamics 365, Facets, NICE CXone, Coupa, SAP Ariba, Oracle Cloud ERP, Workday \n• \nMethodologies & Compliance: Agile/Scrum, Product Management, AI Governance, Responsible AI, HIPAA/GDPR \n• \nIndustry Domains: Healthcare & Life Sciences, Energy & Utilities, Consumer Retail, E-commerce AI, Enterprise Knowledge \nManagement, Contact Center Transformation \n \nPROJECTS \n• \nDeveloped a multi-agent Financial Analysis system using Ollama (local LLMs), LangChain with hybrid RAG retrieval, implemented \nPlanner, Research, and Reporting agents that parse earnings transcripts, extract financial metrics from SEC Edgar filings, benchmark \nagainst competitor data, and autonomously generate executive summaries with \nactionable recommendations validated across 15 company analyses. \n• \nBuilt a RAG-powered Knowledge Copilot using open-source LLMs, ChromaDB, LangChain, FastAPI, and Python to process complex \nenterprise documentation including SOPs, policies, and compliance rules; implemented multi-stage \nretrieval with semantic reranking, answer grounding with source citations, and structured reasoning chains achieving 82% answer \naccuracy on internal knowledge base evaluation set and enabling self-service knowledge access \nfor operational teams. \n• \nBuilt an Autonomous Resume Intelligence & ATS Scoring system using open-source LLMs (Ollama), sentence-transformer embeddings, \nMilvus, LangGraph, and Python; designed multi-agent pipeline with Parsing, JD Matching, Skills Gap Analysis, and ATS Compliance \nagents that extract structured resume data, compute semantic similarity against job descriptions, perform keyword-based ATS scoring, \nidentify missing qualifications, and generate improvement recommendation tested across 50+ resume-JD pairs with 85% alignment to \nrecruiter assessments. \n\n        \n        Analyze the resume against the JD. Provide a JSON response with the following structure:\n        {\n            "match_score": <int 0-100>,\n            "swot_analysis": {\n                "strengths": ["list of strings"],\n                "weaknesses": ["list of strings"],\n                "opportunities": ["list of strings"],\n                "threats": ["list of strings"]\n            },\n            "recommendations": [\n                {\n                    "original": "<exact sentence from resume>",\n                    "suggested": "<rewritten sentence optimized for ATS and impact>",\n                    "reason": "<brief explanation>"\n                }\n            ]\n        }\n        Return ONLY valid JSON. Do not add markdown formatting like ```json.\n        '}], 'model': 'llama-3.3-70b-versatile', 'response_format': {'type': 'json_object'}, 'temperature': 0.0}}
